meta {
  name: Get club quota
  type: http
  seq: 12
}

get {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/clubs/{{clubId}}/quota
  body: none
  auth: bearer
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{accessToken}}
}

docs {
  Any member. How many downloads the club may make and how many it has used. `remaining` never goes below 0, even when an operator lowers the limit below what's already been used.

  Clubs you are not in return 404 `CLUB_NOT_FOUND`. A club admin **cannot** change the limit: that's an operator action (`PATCH /admin/clubs/:clubId/quota`, Basic auth), so a club can't grant itself more downloads.

  Example response:

  ```json
  {
    "quota": {
      "limit": 100,
      "used": 3,
      "remaining": 97,
      "updatedAt": "2026-10-19T10:53:10.735Z"
    }
  }
  ```

  The count never resets; it covers the club's whole lifetime.
}
